+Production installs are named **Lorca** and use `app.lorca`; development installs are named **Lorca Dev** and use `app.lorca.dev`. They are separate applications on macOS, Windows, Linux, iOS, and Android. The production CLI stores its account under `~/.dots` and listens on `4862`, while the desktop-app development build sets `LORCA_HOME=~/.dots-dev` and listens on `4863`. On phones the distinct application ids give each build its own OS sandbox, and the core uses `lorca/core` or `lorca-dev/core` inside that sandbox. Their iOS keychain groups are `group.app.lorca` and `group.app.lorca.dev`.
 
